    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const text = $input.item.json.output[0].content[0].text;\nconst job = $('Code in JavaScript1').item.json;\n\nlet scored;\ntry {\n  scored = JSON.parse(text);\n} catch (e) {\n  scored = { eligible: false, eligibility_reason: 'JSON parse error', score: 0, matching_skills: '', missing_skills: '', match_reason: 'JSON parse error' };\n}\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...job,\n    eligible: scored.eligible === true,\n    eligibility_reason: scored.eligibility_reason || '',\n    score: typeof scored.score === 'number' ? scored.score : 0,\n    matching_skills: scored.matching_skills || '',\n    missing_skills: scored.missing_skills || '',\n    match_reason: scored.match_reason || '',\n    cover_draft: ''\n  }\n};\n"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -3472,
        464
      ],
      "id": "9132f385-80aa-4008-a368-5c720c62910a",
      "name": "Parse Score"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "GPT-4O-MINI"
        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are a job match scorer. Evaluate the posting below against the candidate profile and respond with JSON only \u2014 no markdown, no explanation.\n\nCANDIDATE PROFILE:\n- Skills: JavaScript, TypeScript, React, Next.js, Node.js, n8n workflow automation, LLM APIs (OpenAI/Anthropic), Docker, MCP servers\n- Level: Junior \u2014 treat all listed skills as current capabilities\n- Location: Berlin\n- Target: Junior AI Automation Engineer roles\n- Availability: full-time employment only\n- Status: career transition back into tech after a 3-year break \u2014 not a student\n\nSTEP 1 \u2014 ELIGIBILITY (structural check only):\nSet eligible: false ONLY if one of these three structural conditions is explicitly present in the posting:\n  1. Employment type is Werkstudent, Praktikum, Working student, internship, or Ausbildung \u2014 candidate needs full-time employment\n  2. The job title contains Senior, Lead, Principal, Head, or Manager \u2014 OR the posting explicitly states a numeric years requirement (e.g. '5+ years', 'mindestens 4 Jahre')\n  3. The role requires a specific credential the candidate cannot have (e.g. medical license, law bar, PhD required)\n\nSet eligible: true in ALL other cases, including:\n- Domain or industry mismatch (marketing, finance, operations, etc.) \u2014 skill mismatch is what score is for\n- 'professional / experienced' or 'berufserfahren' job types \u2014 these are eligible: true by default, they do not imply a seniority bar\n- Roles that are a bad fit but are full-time and open to non-students\n\nIf eligible: false, eligibility_reason must quote the exact phrase from the posting that triggered the condition (e.g. 'Working student', 'Senior Engineer', '5+ years required'). Do not paraphrase \u2014 quote verbatim.\nIf eligible: true, eligibility_reason should be a short confirmation (e.g. 'Full-time role, no structural barrier').\n\nSTEP 2 \u2014 SCORING (only after eligibility):\n- Ineligible roles (eligible: false) must receive score: 0\n- Score 7-10 only for junior or entry-level roles with strong technical skill match\n- Score based on skill and domain match only \u2014 not on eligibility\n- Eligible roles with poor skill match should score 1-3, not be marked ineligible\n\nJOB POSTING:\nTitle: {{ $json.title }}\nCompany: {{ $json.company }}\nTags: {{ $json.tags }}\nJob type: {{ $json.job_types }}\nDescription: {{ $json.description_raw.slice(0, 1500) }}\n\nRespond with exactly this JSON structure:\n{\n  \"eligible\": <true or false>,\n  \"eligibility_reason\": \"<verbatim quote from posting if ineligible, or short confirmation if eligible>\",\n  \"score\": <integer 1-10, or 0 if ineligible>,\n  \"matching_skills\": \"<comma-separated skills from the posting that match the candidate>\",\n  \"missing_skills\": \"<comma-separated skills the posting requires but the candidate lacks>\",\n  \"match_reason\": \"<one sentence explaining the score>\"\n}"
            }
